    <div class="legal-content">
      <div class="container text-container">
        <div class="callout-box">
          <strong>Privacy First Principle</strong>
          Voca is built on the principle that your financial records belong exclusively to you. Your receipts, expenses, and voice recordings are processed on your device and synced only to your personal Apple iCloud container. We do not operate external tracking databases or sell personal information to third parties.
        </div>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
          <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Voca ("we", "our", or "the app") collects, processes, and protects your information when you use the Voca iOS application. By downloading or using Voca, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2. Data Collection and Processing</h2>
          <p>We believe in minimal data collection. Voca processes data across three distinct categories:</p>

          <h3>A. Financial Transactions and Ledger Data</h3>
          <p>All transaction records (merchant names, amounts, tax totals, currency codes, dates, and category tags) are stored locally on your device via Apple SwiftData. If you enable iCloud sync, this database synchronizes directly with your private Apple CloudKit database container (<code>iCloud.com.voca.expense.Voca</code>). This data is encrypted in transit and at rest by Apple. Voca developers and operators cannot read or inspect your financial transactions.</p>

          <h3>B. Camera and Receipt Images</h3>
          <p>When you scan receipts using the in-app camera or choose images from your photo library, Optical Character Recognition (OCR) is performed entirely on your device using Apple Vision framework. Receipt images are analyzed on-device to extract totals and line items. Raw receipt images are not sent to any external server.</p>

          <h3>C. Voice Expense Logging and Siri Shortcuts</h3>
          <p>When you use hands-free voice logging or Siri AppIntents (e.g. "Hey Siri, log $15 for lunch"), your voice input is processed on your device using Apple Speech Recognition and Siri framework. Audio files are not uploaded to Voca servers or retained after processing.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>3. Third-Party Services and Telemetry</h2>
          <p>Voca limits third-party code strictly to platform utilities required for monetization and advertising:</p>

          <h3>A. Apple StoreKit 2 (In-App Purchases)</h3>
          <p>Subscription and purchase processing is handled entirely by Apple through StoreKit 2. When you purchase Voca Pro (Monthly, 3-Month, or Annual), Apple securely processes your payment. Voca receives only cryptographically signed transaction verification tokens to activate Pro features on your device. We never receive or store your credit card or billing details.</p>

          <h3>B. Google AdMob (Free Plan Only)</h3>
          <p>For users on the Free Plan, Voca displays non-intrusive advertisements (App Open, Interstitial, and optional Rewarded Ads for bonus receipt scans) powered by the Google Mobile Ads SDK (v12.x). Depending on your iOS App Tracking Transparency (ATT) selection, Google AdMob may collect device identifiers (such as IDFA if permitted) to serve ads. You can manage or revoke tracking permissions anytime in iOS Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Tracking.</p>
          <p><strong>Note for Voca Pro Subscribers:</strong> When you subscribe to Voca Pro, all advertising SDK requests are completely shut down. No ads are loaded or displayed, and ad tracking is disabled.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>4. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
          <p>Because your transaction records live locally on your device and in your private iCloud container:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>In-App Deletion:</strong> Deleting an expense transaction in Voca immediately deletes the record from your device and synchronizes the deletion across all devices connected to your Apple ID.</li>
            <li><strong>App Uninstallation:</strong> Removing Voca from your iOS device deletes all local data immediately.</li>
            <li><strong>iCloud Removal:</strong> You can purge your entire synchronized Voca database at any time by navigating to iOS Settings &gt; [Your Apple ID] &gt; iCloud &gt; Manage Storage &gt; Voca &gt; Delete Data.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>5. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>Voca does not knowingly collect or solicit personal information from children under the age of 13. If you believe that a child under 13 has provided information through the app, please contact us immediately so we can assist in removing the data.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>6. Your Rights (GDPR and CCPA Compliance)</h2>
          <p>Under international privacy regulations including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), you retain the following rights:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Right of Access &amp; Portability:</strong> You can export your entire transaction history at any time in standard RFC-4180 CSV or formatted PDF format from the Reports tab in Voca.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Erasure:</strong> You can delete all your records directly within the app or through your iCloud storage settings.</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> We do not discriminate against users who exercise their privacy rights.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>7. Updates to This Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect product updates or legal adjustments. When updates occur, the "Last Updated" date at the top of this document will be revised. Continued use of Voca after any updates represents acceptance of the revised policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or your data, please contact our privacy compliance team:</p>
          <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:privacy@voca.app">privacy@voca.app</a></p>
          <p><strong>Support Page:</strong> <a href="support.html">voca.app/support</a></p>
        </section>
